  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5015.04 Inspection",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-11-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5015.04 Inspection.\n\n(a) A motor vehicle used for transporting display fireworks shall be inspected daily by the driver prior to operation to determine whether the vehicle is in proper condition for safe transportation of explosive material.\n\n(b) The following shall be inspected:\n\n(1) The fire extinguisher, which shall be filled and ready for immediate use;\n\n(2) All visible electrical wiring underneath the dashboard, the vehicle, or the hood of the vehicle, which shall be protected and securely fastened to prevent short-circuiting;\n\n(3) The chassis, motor, pan, and underside of body, which shall be reasonably clean and free of excess oil and grease;\n\n(4) Fuel tank and feed line;\n\n(5) Brakes, lights, horn, windshield wipers, and steering apparatus; and\n\n(6) Tires, which shall be properly inflated and free of defects.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5000) #6055, eff 7-1-95; amd by #7481, eff 4-25-01; paragraph (b) EXPIRED: 7-1-03; amd by #8117, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04; paragraph (b) EXPIRED: 1-10-05; amd by #8261, eff 1-21-05; amd by #9471, INTERIM, eff 5-15-09, EXPIRED: 11-11-09\n\nNew. #9765-A, eff 8-2-10; ss by #12738, eff 4-30-19",
